{
  "format": "lcir.lesson",
  "formatVersion": 3,
  "id": "multiplexers",
  "title": "Multiplexers: S picks the data",
  "workbench": "circuit",
  "board": "two-to-one-multiplexer",
  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "A **multiplexer** (mux) passes one of its data inputs to the output. The select input **S** chooses which. This 2:1 mux is built from one NOT, two AND gates and one OR gate.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "power",
          "on": true
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "d0",
            "s",
            "d1",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "Set **S** = 0 and **D0** = 1, **D1** = 0. **Y** follows **D0**.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "index": 0,
          "set": [
            1,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "when": "open"
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "d0",
            "s",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Now **D0** = 0, **D1** = 1, **S** = 0. What is **Y**?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Y = 1, because D1 is 1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Y = 0, because S = 0 picks D0",
          "right": true
        }
      ],
      "answer": "**S** = 0 picks **D0**, which is 0. **D1** = 1 is ignored, so **Y** = 0.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "index": 1,
          "set": [
            0,
            0,
            1
          ],
          "when": "reveal"
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "d0",
            "d1",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Flip **S** to 1 with **D0** = 0 and **D1** = 1. What is **Y**?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Y = 0, because D0 is 0"
        },
        {
          "text": "Y = 1, because S = 1 picks D1",
          "right": true
        }
      ],
      "answer": "**S** = 1 picks **D1**, which is 1. **D0** is ignored, so **Y** = 1.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "index": 2,
          "set": [
            0,
            1,
            1
          ],
          "when": "reveal"
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "s",
            "d1",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "Why it works: the NOT gate makes **NOT S** for the upper AND, so AND0 passes **D0** only when **S** = 0. The lower AND passes **D1** only when **S** = 1. The OR gate merges them. As an equation, **Y** = **NOT S**·**D0** + **S**·**D1**.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "ns",
            "and0",
            "and1",
            "or"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "**D0** = 1, **S** = 1, **D1** = 0. What is **Y**?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Y = 1, because D0 is 1"
        },
        {
          "text": "Y = 0, because S = 1 picks D1",
          "right": true
        }
      ],
      "answer": "**S** = 1 selects **D1** = 0. The 1 on **D0** is blocked by AND0, whose other input is **NOT S** = 0.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "index": 3,
          "set": [
            1,
            1,
            0
          ],
          "when": "reveal"
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "and0",
            "and1",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Both data inputs are 1: **D0** = 1, **D1** = 1, **S** = 0. Does **S** change **Y**?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "No, Y = 1 for either S",
          "right": true
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes, Y = 0 when S = 0"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes, Y = 0 when S = 1"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "Whichever input **S** picks, it is a 1, so **Y** = 1. The select only matters when **D0** and **D1** differ.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "row",
          "index": 4,
          "set": [
            1,
            0,
            1
          ],
          "when": "reveal"
        },
        {
          "kind": "highlight",
          "components": [
            "d0",
            "d1",
            "s",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "A mux is also a lookup table: **S** is the address and each data input holds a stored bit. A bigger mux with n select lines picks one of 2^n stored bits. Step through the rest of the rows with `]`.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "kind": "tab",
          "tab": "sequence"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
